//! A resin calibrator (#78): a test piece generated by code, the
//! measurements a person reads off the printed piece with calipers alone
//! (drill bits help, when there are some), and the fit that turns them into
//! numbers a slicer can use.
//!
//! The first piece is the XY coupon ([`coupon`]): blocks of three sizes,
//! holes through it, pins, slits and a column standing on the plate. Its blocks, read in
//! X and in Y, separate the **scale** of the print from the **offset** of its
//! walls ([`fit`]); the holes, pins and slits say how much light bleeds; the
//! column measures the elephant's foot.
//!
//! Nothing here is copied from other calibration tools: the geometry is
//! drawn here, from the published physics (Jacobs' working curve, light
//! bleeding into the walls), and so are the pictures of each step
//! ([`drawing`]).
//!
//! # Units
//!
//! Millimetres throughout.

pub mod coupon;
pub mod drawing;
pub mod fit;

pub use coupon::{Coupon, Feature, Mesh};
pub use drawing::{Step, picture};
pub use fit::{AxisFit, Doubt, Exposure, Slit, Verdict, XyReadings, XyResult};
